 "about_text": "Rajiv Menon Contemporary is a Los Angeles gallery founded in 2023 by gallerist Rajiv Menon, who holds a PhD from New York University in global media and visual culture. The program centers on emerging and diasporic South Asian artists, aiming to expand collecting audiences within diasporic communities and to place new voices into museums and private collections. Initially operating from a Sunset Boulevard space, the gallery opened a permanent home on North Highland Avenue in 2025. Exhibitions have included thematic group shows exploring South Asian regional identity, such as a Kerala-focused Onam exhibition, alongside presentations at international art fairs. The gallery positions itself as a hub connecting South Asia and its diaspora with the broader Los Angeles art world, emphasizing education and connoisseurship alongside commercial representation.",
